<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">This time last week, Football Daily romant=
icised a continental renaissance of sorts. The arrival of J=C3=BCrgen Klopp=
, Zinedine Zidane and Xavi Hern=C3=A1ndez on the international management s=
cene <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLME=
mFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgk9Ca28IB7Zvz4i4KwIQ=
d3sk_Qtv_7z-BewgwGZh0C3LU6A3Gi7HXnrv5AWLkmqSEnADapBp5ZBpUhjqJluODt98H3o9oNr=
tPejan4qkV3igPKHaYv61E9umUYhEf7vphe1Tzw28PlAWQr6empKocYambmCTv78OjTq3koEdng=
cskF5l9LDfqFSUQoDLX6ua9G1renSt_Ta2C5BUd1eEO-ISTX5FGSFxaj3Kfv0rKEeI/4ug/wRbF=
aVZIR4unXi2RBfteLQ/h28/h001.AOhLzVNToltkmAN2S3z4RBfuqYKAn8O4VsaQ4Gx8i64" st=
yle=3D"color: #0077B6;">piqued our interest</a>. We were also impressed by =
the clanging brass stones of Roberto Mancini, who returned to the Italy eje=
ctor-seat three years after abruptly pulling the lever and abandoning his c=
ountry in order to take the Saudi riyal. Two games in and it=E2=80=99s time=
 to appraise the respective early efforts of this glitzy A-list quartet of =
trophy-hoarding aristocrats, one of whom has had a somewhat chastening intr=
oduction to life in the international lane. Oh J=C3=BCrgen!</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Having begun his reign as Germany head coa=
ch by warning the national press not to intrude on his family=E2=80=99s pri=
vacy, Klopp was forced instead to contend with their coverage of him pickin=
g a 44-man squad in order to speed up =E2=80=9Cthe process of opening the d=
oor for many new faces=E2=80=9D as part of his plan to revolutionise the Ge=
rman squad. =E2=80=9CThere=E2=80=99s still plenty of room for improvement,=
=E2=80=9D he honked after his side drew his first match in charge <a href=
=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18I=
RyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg4D28efg-wqeJSpo_spS5SVPVuoXC9vk=
xPojG559gDZYnGsGxO2zPfc6BKPWea67c5KVB-nCq980bHxruqOmCEUm3hk1ymEXMibDbZOBnh4=
yB0Q89vBi1qqjKL2osLvX-mxoBVOj7FHn7dYG2JRfypWf1X2yEr2_7sC7hQnYeTL4JZoZFBFP92=
Rg6P9vUfmFr7l1EiIU-xE8qKl7j2Rlpk0drJ3amgxAuy2WdHUuacqk/4ug/wRbFaVZIR4unXi2R=
BfteLQ/h29/h001.Rf23fv21Y_R4OjbJpOpvy3YJqN9wmiLDzA0ZtU5HdK4" style=3D"color=
: #0077B6;">against Xavi=E2=80=99s Netherlands</a>, before failing to show =
any in a historic <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/=
u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgs68SKl=
MtwoD8hee50RqAsNrz73gIiBy_lfDtYEBhFC4XCpV2XaeFvIupOXKI0wpxDYDgyTsTyEtYHFksw=
j9kVK7Edh2SJfoMk1RHpbIr3eLGlAX66ph7iFOFP0ZPfVVPakOy9rtIt4NrVaUVVIodDaI47sdM=
04GK4Zo_BXqbLlwucO_bgx7Aev9eB30yDwy6qp6lg_X7Wng_BcCszaGgwWvkUf3h-IsnptgOyYd=
B7cTgt6ZnfFga71tKY1KsZ13Y/4ug/wRbFaVZIR4unXi2RBfteLQ/h30/h001.4FGF4zF0T977m=
L7_a7OeL0jpn-vh0usKOBbWmr25k6w" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">first-ever defeat=
 by Greece</a>. =E2=80=9CThe lineup, the formation, the many changes =E2=80=
=93 that is all 100% down to me,=E2=80=9D he sighed. =E2=80=9CFootball, tha=
t=E2=80=99s how it is. I don=E2=80=99t think we deserved that, but here we =
are.=E2=80=9D Here we are, being in third place in their Nations League gro=
up and already facing a must(ish)-win match against Serbia to avoid possibl=
e relegation.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Xavi, meanwhile, chalked up his first Neth=
erlands win in Belgrade against Serbia. The Barcelona legend had late callu=
p Mexx Meerdink to thank at the final whistle after the AZ striker scored b=
oth goals in a 2-1 win. Next comes Thursday=E2=80=99s match against the gro=
up-leading Greeks. Responding to suggestions that there were many moments w=
hen the Dutch needed to attack the spaces but didn=E2=80=99t do it, a contr=
ite Xavi confessed, =E2=80=9Cthere were many moments when we needed to atta=
ck the spaces, but we didn=E2=80=99t do it=E2=80=9D. In danger of losing th=
eir global status as dark horses to Greece, Turkey rolled over to give Manc=
ini the first win of his second spell in charge of Italy, who lost to Belgi=
um last week. After being reappointed, the Italian apologised for doing the=
 dirty on the <em>Azzurri</em> first time around in order to take up a lucr=
ative contract with Saudi Arabia. He has since had to face down questions a=
bout another of his former nation state paymasters. After <a href=3D"https:=
//ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fI=
EMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgV4L9PCxkGy79OqZVwbVw-VbgbqxiJqheerq1mM_pw=
S9XxC6hm4uzWjAPxnZcWPigSYujG5lVasJd-_fhrAXZDuDzVe_iqXcslrA9RKkGUTuR8LSqAov7=
pnlZ115jzjO2JX4lBA56kAL_TLfn1d9JfkmiIzFtfr9jLsf5Tf6j2EsrSHdXrm5zdkjHrY_AKeO=
IVc4uYVRmMtVCccFgN2NCercDWW1O-YfrYmFvQOkjgJQ/4ug/wRbFaVZIR4unXi2RBfteLQ/h31=
/h001.C-0KXH8XVdEhn3DUDyICWnI85JzfpF6L_C1a_ifZB5Q" style=3D"color: #0077B6;=
">referring to claims</a> he had a =E2=80=9Cdouble contract=E2=80=9D during=
 his time at Manchester City, Mancini described the current scandal surroun=
ding his former club as =E2=80=9Cnot a problem that concerns me=E2=80=9D.</=
p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">On a night when Michael Kayode marked the =
occasion of becoming the first Brentford player in history to represent Ita=
ly by scoring a goal, Mancini said the 22-year-old =E2=80=9Cwill improve ev=
en more after another year in the Premier League=E2=80=9D. Given his lack o=
f popularity among many Italy fans, whether he=E2=80=99ll still be around t=
o see Kayode blossom remains to be seen. Their next appointment is in Paris=
 on Friday against France, whose manager Zidane is the only one of our four=
 heroes to get off to a perfect start in his new gig. After back-to-back 1-=
0 wins in Turkey and Belgium, the latter won by a sensational Michael Olise=
 solo effort late-doors, Zidane was asked about his meme-worthy touchline c=
elebration that involved a sprint, a little dance and leathering a spare ba=
ll off a cone. =E2=80=9CI saw the ball,=E2=80=9D he giggled. =E2=80=9CI was=
 forced to shoot it, be a bit ridiculous but it doesn=E2=80=99t matter.=E2=
=80=9D Never mind the tactical revolutions of J=C3=BCrgen, Xavi and Roberto=
, when the chips are down just go full Zizou and get it launched.</p>
